[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "French Defence: Advance Variation"]
[Variation "Advance Variation, Paulsen Attack"]
[ECO "C02"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "pawn-chain,d4-pawn"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4...cxd4"]
[Start "advance-qb6 4.c3"]

4... cxd4 5. cxd4 { Take back with the pawn. Now the pawn on d4 is attacked only by pieces, and White can guard it easily. } 5... Nc6 6. Nf3 { Develops and guards d4 again. } 6... Bd7 7. Nc3 { A second knight guards d4 and eyes b5 and a4. } 7... Qb6 8. a3 { Stops ...Bb4, which would pin the knight on c3 and make d4 harder to guard. } 8... Nge7 9. Na4 { Hits the queen and wins a tempo. } 9... Qc7 10. Bd3 { Plan: finish development, castle, and answer ...f6 with exf6 or Bd3. Keep d4 guarded and keep the bishop on c1 for b2. } *
